  Sorting hundreds of domains by hand was the most tedious part of the week, so
  I built a tool to do it in seconds.
draft: false
---
Manually categorising hundreds of domains was always a tedious, repetitive task. So I built an AI-powered tool that does it in seconds.

It handles a single domain check or a bulk upload through Google Sheets, Excel or CSV. Under the hood it uses Python, Pandas, BeautifulSoup and a lightweight text-classification model, built for accuracy, speed and day-to-day use.

It has already saved hours of manual effort and helps the team make decisions faster.

Building it was a good reminder that innovation doesn't always mean big ideas. Sometimes it's about fixing small pains well.
